# AI Coding Tools — shared core, applied to every project
# Credentials, cross-tool conventions and the rules that govern the per-tool
#   blocks. Always applied. The credential lines cover tools this project may
#   not use: a stray inert line costs nothing, a committed token costs a
#   rotation, and that asymmetry is the whole reason they sit together here.
# Added by /nf-ignore

# Agent credentials — the only files in this asset whose accidental commit
#   cannot be undone without rotating a token. One line each, always worth it.
.claude/.credentials.json
.codex/auth.json
.codex/.env
.opencode/auth.json

# Local conventions
.local/

# MCP server output — runtime artifacts, never team-shared
#   Playwright MCP: screenshots, page snapshots (.yml), scraped page content
.playwright-mcp/

# Skill-sync CLI manifest (openskills / agent-skills-cli). Ignored by DEFAULT
#   only because it can carry private registry URLs; it holds sync decisions and
#   custom_overrides, NOT raw tokens. That cuts both ways: custom_overrides is
#   what stops the next `sync` overwriting locally customized skills, so a team
#   that actually runs the CLI together should UN-IGNORE this and commit it —
#   it is also the only file identifying which skill dirs are generated.
.skillsrc
!.skillsrc.example

# Local agent-tool output directory. Source unconfirmed: observed only on an
#   Antigravity user's checkout, but Antigravity's documented artifact path is
#   ~/.gemini/antigravity/brain/<conversation-id>/, not the project root, and no
#   common test/build tool defaults to a bare artifacts/. Ignored because it is
#   generated locally and has never belonged to a repo's history.
#   Leading slash on purpose: a bare artifacts/ would also swallow a real
#   packages/*/artifacts/ in a workspace repo.
/artifacts/

# Personal-prefix obligation — which directories carry the set, and why.
#   A directory this asset keeps TRACKED needs the user-/private-/hidden-/
#   personal-/me-/*.local* set, or a personal file in it gets committed. The set
#   is emitted for .claude/, .agents/, .agent/, .codex/, .gemini/ and
#   .commandcode/ — the six whose authored contents (rules, skills, agents, hooks, commands) were
#   measured or vendor-documented.
#   It is NOT emitted for .cursor/, .roo/, .kilocode/, .windsurf/, .continue/,
#   .qwen/, .opencode/ or .antigravity/. Not because they are exempt — the same
#   obligation applies the moment a team authors inside one — but because this
#   asset only ignores a connection-config file in each, and none of them was
#   investigated. Adding six globs per directory on assumption is the exact
#   habit that put fifteen inert patterns in here in the first place. Measure
#   first, then add.

# NOT ignored, deliberately — do not "tidy up" by adding these:
#   .claude/ .github/ .codex/rules/ .agents/rules/ .agents/plugins/
#   CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md AGENT.md .mcp.json .github/CODEOWNERS
#   Each holds team-shared files that must stay tracked. A whole-directory entry
#   for any of them overrides the targeted blocks above AND kills the negations,
#   because git never descends into an ignored directory.
#   .mcp.json in particular is the project-scope MCP list, MEANT to be shared.
#   Ignore it only if that repo's copy hardcodes a key inline — check with
#     grep -nE '(sk-|Bearer |ghp_|glpat-|AIza|xox[baprs]-)' .mcp.json
#   and if it hits, the fix is moving the secret to an ${ENV_VAR}, not ignoring
#   the file. Same test before ignoring any *.json/*.toml config in this asset.

# Claude Code — project files
# Applied when Claude Code is detected or selected.
# Added by /nf-ignore

# Claude Code — local/personal only; team-shared stay committed
#   Prefix user-, private-, hidden-, personal-, me- + .local suffix (any depth)
**/.claude/**/user-*
**/.claude/**/private-*
**/.claude/**/hidden-*
**/.claude/**/personal-*
**/.claude/**/me-*
**/.claude/**/*.local*
CLAUDE.local.md
#   me- = "MeOnly": personal-by-default. New project skills are named
#   me-<proj>-<name> so they stay LOCAL unless explicitly unlocked.
#   To share one, add a negation BELOW this line, e.g.:
#     !.claude/skills/me-<proj>-<name>/
#   Runtime state — CC-generated, machine-specific
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scratch*/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/evolve/
.claude/**/*.log
#   agent-memory/ is NOT here on purpose. Anthropic's own file reference badges
#   `.claude/agent-memory/` as COMMITTED: "This directory holds project-scoped
#   subagent memory, meant to be shared with your team. To keep memory out of
#   version control use `memory: local`, which writes to
#   .claude/agent-memory-local/". So the shared one stays tracked and only the
#   -local variant is ignored. An earlier revision had this exactly backwards.
.claude/agent-memory-local/
#   plans/ is documented ONLY under ~/.claude/ (the cleanupPeriodDays table), so
#   by this file's own rule it should live in config-home.gitignore. It is kept
#   here because 10 of 80 measured project .claude/ folders do contain it —
#   likely older CC behaviour — and plan files are disposable output, so hiding
#   them costs nothing. Do not cite it as matching vendor convention.
.claude/plans/
#   Config-dir-only runtime state (sessions/, jobs/, todos/, teams/, statsig/,
#   ide/, debug/, uploads/, history.jsonl, ...) is deliberately NOT here. Those
#   live at the ROOT of the Claude Code config dir, never under a project's
#   .claude/ — measured 0 occurrences across 80 real project .claude/ folders.
#   They moved to config-home.gitignore, which /nf-ignore applies only when run
#   inside the config dir itself, where the correct form is unprefixed
#   (`sessions/`, not `.claude/sessions/`). Do NOT re-add them with a .claude/
#   prefix: that prefix matches nothing in either place.

# Common baseline — language-agnostic, safe for any stack
# Added by /nf-ignore (fast path for projects with no detected stack)

# OS junk
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE — local, personal
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# Logs & temp
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.pid
*.seed
tmp/
temp/

# Dependency dirs (common across ecosystems; harmless if unused)
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Env / secrets — block by default; whitelist examples
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.local

# Local Claude Code overrides (per-machine, not for VCS)
.claude/settings.local.json

.envrc
